From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DVDClock: take m_critSection in GetClock(double&)

Fixes found by the S905X5/CoreELEC driver review:

- F113 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp:69: GetClock(double& absolute) reads Discontinuity() state under the wrong lock; new render-thread callers can see a clock that is hours off

See the review diary (S905X5-DRIVER-REVIEW-DIARY.md) for the defect
analysis and the forum discussion.

final judge sign-off did not run, so this patch still needs a human
read before it is proposed upstream. Not yet exercised on S905X5 hardware.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp
@@ -68,9 +68,12 @@
 
 double CDVDClock::GetClock(double& absolute, bool interpolated /*= true*/)
 {
+  // SystemToPlaying() state is guarded by m_critSection (ErrorAdjust holds it
+  // when calling here); lock order: m_critSection -> m_systemsection.
+  std::unique_lock lock(m_critSection);
   int64_t current = m_videoRefClock->GetTime(interpolated);
 
-  std::unique_lock lock(m_systemsection);
+  std::unique_lock systemLock(m_systemsection);
   absolute = SystemToAbsolute(current);
 
   m_systemAdjust += m_speedAdjust * (current - m_lastSystemTime);
